---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Pip - Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Pip - Atlanta Train Times, the iOS app. No data collected; your trips and rides stay on your iPhone and Apple Watch."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/pip/privacy"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] mb-12">Pip - Atlanta Train Times &middot; Effective October 25, 2026</p>

        <div class="space-y-8 text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">The Short Version</h2>
            <p>Pip does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data. There&rsquo;s no account, no analytics, no ads and no tracking. Your trips and rides never leave your devices.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Data Storage</h2>
            <p>Your trips (the stations, walk time, name and color), your settings, your leave reminders and your ride card are stored locally on your iPhone. They are shared with Pip&rsquo;s own widgets through an App Group on the same device, and your trips with your paired Apple Watch. No data is sent to any server, cloud service, or third party. There are no user accounts and no sign-up required.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Your Location</h2>
            <p>Location is off unless you allow it. If you do, Pip uses your location on your iPhone to put the nearest stations and trips first and to estimate your walk. Your location is never stored by us or sent anywhere. You can turn it off at any time in the iPhone Settings app.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Train Times and Alerts</h2>
            <p>To show live arrivals and service alerts, Pip downloads the transit agency&rsquo;s public train feeds. These requests ask for every train on the system, not for your stations or trips, and include nothing about you. Like any internet request, they reveal your IP address to the server that answers them.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Import</h2>
            <p>Bringing your trips over from our earlier train app reads only the trips that app saved on your device.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Notifications</h2>
            <p>Leave reminders, stop nudges and the Lock Screen countdown are scheduled on your device. If you turn on Alerts on my trips, Pip checks the public alerts now and then in the background and notifies you on your device. Nothing is sent through our servers, and nothing is sent to us.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Analytics &amp; Tracking</h2>
            <p>Pip contains no analytics frameworks, no ad SDKs, no tracking pixels, and no telemetry of any kind. We do not use any third-party services that collect data.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Tips</h2>
            <p>Tips are handled entirely by Apple through the App Store; Pip never sees your payment details or Apple Account.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Your Choices</h2>
            <p>You can delete a trip from the trip&rsquo;s form, turn off the Made it question in Settings, and deleting the app removes all of its data from your device.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Children's Privacy</h2>
            <p>Pip does not knowingly collect any information from anyone, including children under the age of 13.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Changes to This Policy</h2>
            <p>If this policy changes, we will update this page with the new effective date. Since Pip collects no data, meaningful changes are unlikely. Questions? Email <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
